<characters>
  <character>
    <name>Captain Lazlow</name>
    <metatype>Troll</metatype>
    <background>With a neon black centipede coming from the eye socket wrapped around like a scarf around one’s neck, Captain Lazlow proclaims loudly. “We are plumbers of the modern age. Your job is done and you will be taking a 5 minute break. A token of our appreciation for your service.” .. The nickname for the company is the “roaches” \- (say that to their face, and loose a limb), the company name is the Fuchsia Dragons . Previously a private security force part of Ares, the mercenary company is notable for having a unique spirit pact with centipede insect spirits. The company has a "procession of remembrance" where each spirit remembers it's pact and honors the fallen who they now posses. Pact breakers are not remembered and spirits only state their own names. Depending on how the bond is accepted, depends on how completely transformed they are. Oath breakers tend to transform fully, while those who resist become abominations and serve as shock brigade troops With his thuggery out on display, Captain Lazlow opens his great white mitts, signaling the rest of the company to show the recruits the basics of construction, erecting a strong roof that will be impenetrable to the rifle fire of the horde. They all gather on a platform made of two 6 foot by 6 foot pieces of rebar held together by a girdle of plywood and glass. This is the gangplank to the abandoned boat below. Captain Lazlow tells them that it was an over priced helipad and he wants this pier converted into a fortress. I then hear the whole crew gathering by the gangplank to converse,</background>
